sections.markdown:
The class bag bound is still an explicit intermediate hypothesis. This
combines the proved probability estimates and sampled width obstruction;
it does not yet derive the class bound from separators.

The coordinate type contains exactly the sets of size at most $r+2$;
there are no coordinates for larger sets. The accessor is extended by zero
outside this domain, solely to simplify notation. Every constraint that
uses it supplies a size bound ensuring that it reads an actual coordinate.
The vector space and convex hull are over the reals, as in the paper;
the algorithms will use rational points in this space.

proofs.description:
A fixed pair of registered solvers supplies projection certificates and flow
cuts. The protected-cube argument proves completeness of the bounded search;
a size-k subset of any larger independent set excludes false rejection.
